process-gpu-arrays.m's summers spawned on the machine's GPU: three hundred
arrays to one, then one to each of a hundred, and an array and a sum back for
each, read right at the GPU and at the host.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-gpu-arrays.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-gpu-arrays.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PINNED=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK:0 wrong of 300
CHECK-NEXT:0 wrong of 100
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of host memory for devices' messages are allocated
